note('s01-dialog','Dell Cameron and Yulia Almazova, “Leak Exposes Members of Peter Thiel’s Secretive ‘Dialog’ Society,” WIRED, June 16, 2026, https://www.wired.com/story/leak-exposes-members-of-peter-thiels-secretive-dialog-society/; and Dell Cameron, Dhruv Mehrotra and Yulia Almazova, “How the Peter Thiel-Linked Dialog Club Secretly Ranks Its Members,” WIRED, June 18, 2026, https://www.wired.com/story/how-peter-thiels-private-dialog-club-secretly-ranks-its-members/. Source houses `wired-2026-dialog-exposed` and `wired-2026-dialog-rankings`, p001 in each. Primary publisher text and membership/guest distinction checked October 4, 2026; current offices/sectors wording is preserved. Novara remains a supplied corroborating lead, not a newly acquired witness in this pass.')
note('s01-mkultra','United States Senate, Project MKULTRA, the CIA’s Program of Research in Behavioral Modification, joint hearing, 95th Congress, 1st session, August 3, 1977, https://www.intelligence.senate.gov/sites/default/files/hearings/95mkultra.pdf. Source house `senate-1977-project-mkultra-hearing`, p001: Kennedy print p.3 (digital page 7) and Turner print pp.4–6 (digital pages 8–10), on the 1973 destruction order and surviving financial folders. The selected primary passages do not independently identify Cameron/Subproject 68; that specific historical attribution remains to be sourced separately.')
note('s01-mkultra-2026','House Committee on Oversight, Task Force on the Declassification of Federal Secrets, “Mind Control and Accountability: Uncovering the Truth of the CIA’s MKULTRA Project,” June 30, 2026, https://oversight.house.gov/hearing/mind-control-and-accountability-uncovering-the-truth-of-the-cias-mkultra-project/. Stephen Kinzer’s three-page submitted testimony is https://oversight.house.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Kinzer-Written-Testimony.pdf; source house `kinzer-2026-mkultra-house-testimony`, p001, especially p.2. The actual date is June 30 and title ends “Project”; current body/date correction is separately proposed, never silently applied. Oral proceedings, Poisoner in Chief, and the National Security Archive item are separate acquisitions; the written testimony does not contain the draft’s prosecution/compensation assertion.')
note('s01-epstein-redaction','Todd Blanche, December 19, 2025 letter to Congress on Epstein files production, United States Department of Justice, https://www.justice.gov/opa/media/1434851/dl, pp.1–4 (redaction categories p.2; EFTA Bates numbers p.3). Source house `doj-2025-epstein-production-letter`, p001. All six pages checked October 4, 2026. This source establishes the Department’s release process and attributed rationale; it does not by itself establish the current prose’s scale-of-redaction or protected-co-conspirator conclusions. M05’s Martin proposal is a separate exact record, EFTA01040587, whose official PDF remained behind the DOJ age-verification redirect during this pass.')
